{# This round's stimulus: the full transition table, the start state, the
   input string, and one question line.

   Supervisor voice (2026-09-10, prompt revision v2): the body opens
   ``ROUND N.`` on its own line and each section carries a ``LABEL:``
   header, the same shape ``tasks/signal_game/observation_puzzle.j2``
   uses, so the observation, the history block and the ransom call all
   call a round by the same word.

   Short by design (§3.2): the table is one row per state, the input is
   one line in groups of four, the question is one line. Nothing is
   repeated from the system rules -- ``n_steps`` is the single number
   the agent would otherwise have to count off the string itself.

   Variables:
     turn_number   : int  -- the round
     n_states      : int  -- how many states
     first_state   : str  -- "q0"
     last_state    : str  -- e.g. "q4"
     start_state   : str  -- the state the machine starts in
     rows          : list[str] -- one transition row per state
     word          : str  -- the input, already grouped in fours
     n_steps       : int  -- how many symbols the input has
     question_kind : str  -- "final" | "count"
     count_state   : str  -- the state a "count" round asks about
#}ROUND {{ turn_number }}.
THE MACHINE: {{ n_states }} states, {{ first_state }} to {{ last_state }}. It starts in {{ start_state }}.
TRANSITIONS:
{% for row in rows %}  {{ row }}
{% endfor %}THE INPUT: {{ n_steps }} symbols, read left to right.
  {{ word }}
{% if question_kind == "count" %}QUESTION: how many times is the machine in {{ count_state }}, counting the starting state and the state after each symbol?{% else %}QUESTION: which state is the machine in after the whole input has been read?{% endif %}
